steps.context:
Write a monthly review summary to /tmp/monthly_review_event.md using your FILE EDITOR TOOL (not a terminal command). Format:

# Monthly Review — {month} {year}

## What Was Built
{concrete list — shipped features, milestones, decisions}

## What to Stop
{things identified for removal or deprioritisation}

## What Deserves More Focus
{underinvested areas worth doubling down on}

## Direction Check
{is the overall direction still correct? what changed?}

## Recurring Themes
{patterns from interrupts, blockers, energy mismatches this month}

Then run: `bash .exocortex/scripts/create_event.sh --body-file /tmp/monthly_review_event.md` followed by `bash .exocortex/scripts/sync_event_to_vault.sh $(ls -t .exocortex/events/*.md 2>/dev/null | head -1)`. Show one line: '✓ Monthly review saved and synced' or '✓ Monthly review saved (sync skipped — no RAG key)'.
